---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";

const updated = "November 7, 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Dee7 Studio"
  description="What dee7studio.com collects, why, which cookies it sets, and how to change your choice at any time. Plain language, no surprises."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Privacy Policy", path: "/privacy" }]}
>
  <section class="legal">
    <div class="container legal__inner">
      <header class="legal__head" data-rise>
        <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
        <h1 class="legal__title">Privacy policy.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Short version: we count visits to learn what helps, we keep the
          contact form simple, and you decide about cookies. Last updated {updated}.
        </p>
        <nav class="legal__toc" aria-label="On this page">
          <a href="#who">Who we are</a>
          <a href="#collect">What we collect</a>
          <a href="#cookies">Cookies and analytics</a>
          <a href="#third-parties">Other services</a>
          <a href="#rights">Your rights</a>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <div class="legal__body">
        <section id="who">
          <h2>Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            {SITE.name} ("we") runs {SITE.url.replace("https://", "")}. For anything in this policy,
            write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="collect">
          <h2>What we collect</h2>
          <h3>If you contact us</h3>
          <p>
            When you send the contact form, we store what you typed (your name,
            email, and anything you add about your project) in a database
            hosted by Fillout (Zite), our form and data provider, and email a copy
            to our inbox through Resend, our email delivery provider. We use it
            only to reply and to scope your project, and keep it for as long as
            the conversation or a resulting project needs it. If the form
            cannot send, it opens a pre-filled email in your own mail app
            instead. You can ask us to delete your enquiry at any time.
          </p>
          <h3>When you visit</h3>
          <p>
            Our host, Cloudflare, processes your IP address and basic request
            details to deliver the pages and keep the site secure. We do not
            use this to identify you.
          </p>
          <p>
            Google Analytics counts visits and shows us which pages and calls to
            action work. What it can store depends on your choice, explained
            next.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="cookies">
          <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
          <p>
            We use Google Analytics 4, loaded through Google Tag Manager, under
            Google Consent Mode. Nothing else on this site sets cookies for
            advertising or tracking, and we do not run ads.
          </p>

          <h3>If you accept</h3>
          <p>
            Google Analytics sets two first-party cookies and uses them to
            recognise a returning browser, so visits, sessions and journeys are
            measured accurately.
          </p>
          <div class="legal__table-wrap">
            <table class="legal__table">
              <thead>
                <tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>_ga</code></td><td>Tells one browser from another</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>_ga_{SITE.ga4Id.replace("G-", "")}</code></td><td>Keeps session state</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h3>If you decline</h3>
          <p>
            Google Analytics sets no cookies and stores no identifier in your
            browser. We still count that the visit happened. Google Tag Manager
            sends a small anonymous signal with the page address, page title,
            referrer, approximate location, and browser and device type. It has
            no persistent ID, so it cannot follow you from visit to visit. We
            use these signals only for totals, such as how many people viewed a
            page.
          </p>

          <h3>Your choice</h3>
          <p>
            We store your answer in your browser (local storage, key
            <code>dee7-consent</code>) for 180 days, so we do not ask on every
            page. This record is needed to respect your choice and is not used
            for tracking. Change your mind at any time:
          </p>
          <p>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary" data-consent-open>
              Open cookie settings
            </button>
          </p>
          <p>
            Cookie settings are also in the footer of every page. You can
            delete the cookies above in your browser at any time.
          </p>

          <h3>Legal basis</h3>
          <p>
            Analytics cookies rely on your consent. Anonymous visit counting
            without cookies, hosting and security rely on our legitimate
            interest in running and improving a business website, which has
            minimal impact on you. Replying to your email relies on taking
            steps at your request.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="third-parties">
          <h2>Other services this site loads</h2>
          <p>
            These providers receive your IP address when your browser fetches
            their files, because that is how the web works:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts and delivers the site.</li>
            <li><strong>Google</strong> (Tag Manager, Analytics) as described above, and <strong>Google Fonts</strong> for the Inter and Instrument Serif typefaces.</li>
            <li><strong>Fontshare</strong> (Indian Type Foundry) for the Clash Display typeface.</li>
            <li><strong>Sanity</strong> serves some article and project images.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Some of these providers are based in the United States. They
            transfer data under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or Standard
            Contractual Clauses.
          </p>
          <p>
            Links to other websites, such as client sites in our portfolio, are
            governed by their own policies.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="rights">
          <h2>Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You can ask us for access to, correction of, deletion of, or a copy
            of your personal data, and object to or restrict how we use it. You
            can withdraw consent whenever you like using the cookie settings
            above. Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and
            we will answer within one month. If you are unhappy with our
            answer, you can complain to your local data protection authority.
          </p>
          <p>
            This site is not aimed at children, and we do not knowingly collect
            their data.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="changes">
          <h2>Changes</h2>
          <p>
            If we change this policy, we update the date at the top. If a change
            affects what we collect, we ask for your choice again.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-block: var(--space-8) var(--space-section);
  }

  .legal__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 4fr 7fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .legal__head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    position: sticky;
    top: 104px;
  }

  .legal__title {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.4vw, 56px);
  }

  .legal__toc {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .legal__toc a {
    color: var(--muted);
    transition: color var(--ease);
  }

  .legal__toc a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-text);
  }

  .legal__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .legal__body section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    scroll-margin-top: 104px;
  }

  .legal__body h2 {
    font-size: clamp(26px, 3vw, 34px);
  }

  .legal__body h3 {
    font-size: 19px;
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
  }

  .legal__body p,
  .legal__body li {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .legal__body ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    max-width: 640px;
  }

  .legal__body strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .legal__body p a,
  .legal__body li a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-skip-ink: none;
    transition: text-decoration-color var(--ease);
  }

  .legal__body p a:hover,
  .legal__body li a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent-text);
  }

  .legal__body code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--tint);
    color: var(--ink);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .legal__table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--surface);
    max-width: 640px;
  }

  .legal__table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .legal__table th,
  .legal__table td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--muted);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .legal__table th {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .legal__table tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .legal__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-6);
    }

    .legal__head {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
